WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:03.000
Computed quarter-full bottle at a prescribed tilt. Left: water immobilized. Right: water settles with a horizontal surface. Gold marks combined CG and weight; pink marks the rim pivot.

00:03.000 --> 00:05.000
Hold at 20.98 degrees: the immobilized payload still restores upright, while gravity drives the freely settled liquid case farther over. Its critical angle is lower.

00:05.000 --> 00:10.000
Settled-water threshold: 20.72 degrees. Immobilized threshold: 21.23 degrees. The imposed tilt continues and returns; this is not a freely falling, spilling, or sloshing simulation.
